{"status":200,"location":"https://zodiacs-4qqy7ml63-zodiacsofficial.vercel.app/developers/","title":"Developer Tools — Local Charts, Sky Data & Embeds | Zodiacs.org","footerCount":1,"footerClasses":["zfooter"],"text":"SKIP TO CONTENT\nZODIACS·ORG\nTools\nSigns\nToday\nLearn\nHoroscopes\nSaved charts\n/\nASTROFOLIO\nFor developers and AI agents\nCharts, data, and embeds.\n\nUnpublished candidate · 0.1.1-rc.6\n\nCalculate locally\n\nUse TypeScript or JavaScript for tropical charts, transits, and synastry in your own browser or Node.js app. Core calculations make no network requests.\n\nAvailable · public files\n\nFetch shared sky data\n\nRead the daily sky and dated events as JSON. No account or API key; check the edition and snapshot before displaying them.\n\nAvailable · hosted embeds\n\nEmbed a tool\n\nChoose a Moon, sky, or mini birth-chart iframe. Set its theme and size, and keep the built-in Zodiacs.org credit.\n\nPlanned · no public endpoint\n\nUse hosted computation\n\nA personalized chart API is planned. Its input contract, privacy limits, and release approval remain open.\n\nRun the three examples: local natal chart, personalized transits, and a publisher widget.\n\nCompare support, runtime requirements, and known limits before choosing an integration.\n\nThe optional ownership SDK is a separate, read-only integration for registry verification and public ownership reads. Charts, sky data, and widgets do not require it or a wallet.\n\nShared sky data\n\nThe computed dates behind this site's calendars — today's sky, the weeks ahead, retrograde windows, stations, sign ingresses, moon phases, eclipses, and exact aspects — are published as versioned JSON. The files are static, cached at the edge, and open to any origin. There is no key or signup. These files contain no personal birth data: they describe the shared sky, and chart calculation stays on the device.\n\nQuick start\nconst response = await fetch('https://zodiacs.org/api/v1/sky/today.json', {\n  cache: 'no-cache',\n  signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000),\n});\nif (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Sky request failed: HTTP ${response.status}`);\n\nconst sky = await response.json();\nif (sky?.schema !== 'zodiacs.sky-api.today.v1'\n  || typeof sky.date !== 'string'\n  || typeof sky.snapshotAt !== 'string'\n  || typeof sky.summary !== 'string'\n  || !Array.isArray(sky.bodies)\n  || sky.bodies.length === 0\n  || sky.bodies.some((body) => !body\n    || typeof body !== 'object'\n    || typeof body.body !== 'string'\n    || typeof body.position !== 'string'\n    || typeof body.retrograde !== 'boolean')) {\n  throw new Error('Unexpected sky payload');\n}\n\nconst today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nif (sky.date !== today) {\n  throw new Error(`Sky edition ${sky.date} is not curr","errors":[]}
